# Backend & Data

## Supabase

- **Default:** cloud project (`EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` + `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`). See `supabase/README.md`.
- Mobile uses **publishable** keys (`sb_publishable_...`); **secret** keys (`sb_secret_...`) are server-only (`apps/api`, Edge Functions) — never in the mobile bundle
- Migrations only in `supabase/migrations/` — never hand-edit production
- Push schema: `supabase link` then `supabase db push`
- Seed curated starter data: `supabase db query --linked -f supabase/seed.sql` (cloud) or `supabase db reset` (local Docker)
- Sync auth settings (anonymous sign-ins): `supabase config push` after link
- Row Level Security on every user-data table
- Onboarding works guest-first; auth optional until dashboard

## API (Express)

- Validate all request bodies with Zod middleware
- Separate endpoints: `/motifs/detect` (deterministic) vs `/puzzles/generate` (LLM)
- Return `{ data }` on success, `{ error, code }` on failure
- Idempotent peek recording: dedupe by `(match_id, ply)` (planned server); client today uses `positionKeyFromFen` in `guestStore.addPeekEvent`

## Security

- LLM and service keys server-side only — never in mobile bundle
- `.env.local` for secrets (user-managed — agents must not read, write, or commit); provide `.env.example` with placeholder keys only
- Rate-limit LLM templating endpoint

## Key Tables

`profiles`, `heatmap_ledger`, `puzzle_bank` are implemented. Planned match work may add `peek_events` and `matches`. See `heatmap-analytics` skill for ledger semantics.

## Peek → Puzzle

Match peek (client) → `guestStore.peekEvents` (deduped by position) → `peekPuzzles` for daily drill (up to 2/session). Remaining daily slots come from runtime generators (`selectDailyCategoryPuzzles`); optional `puzzle_bank` top-up when Supabase is linked. Bulk export: `npm run generate:puzzles` in chess-core. Server-side peek → bank insert remains optional Phase 4 cache.
